+"""Torch-native k-pool DSA indexer for GLM-5.3-Flash on HPU (Phase 3b).
+
+Semantics follow the HF reference (``Glm5NextTextIndexer``), verified token-for-token
+by ``scripts/test_dsa_select.py``:
+
+* indexer q = wq_b(q_c) [T, H, D]; k = layer_norm(wk(x)) [T, D]; gate = x @ gate_w.T [T, D];
+  w = weights_proj(x) [T, H].
+* keys are pooled ``kpool`` (=4) consecutive tokens at a time, starting at position 0:
+  pool_key = sum(softmax(gate + ape) * k).
+* index score(t, p) = sum_h w[t,h] * H^-0.5 * relu(scale * q[t,h] . pool_key[p]).
+* a pool is selectable by query t iff it is complete and its last token <= t.
+* the top ``topk / kpool`` (=512) pools are selected (2048 tokens) plus the incomplete tail
+  pool [kpool * floor((t+1)/kpool), t] (0..3 tokens, always includes t itself).
+* for t + 1 <= topk + kpool - 1 (2051) every visible token is selected, so dense MLA is exact.
+
+Everything is static-shape: bucketed prompt length L (multiple of kpool), padded decode block
+lists. Sparsity is applied as an additive -inf bias on the existing dense HPU attention
+kernels (prefill: [B, 1, L, L] bias for the fused SDPA; decode: per-block [N, block_size]
+bias for flat paged attention), so the numerics of the attention itself are unchanged.
 """
 from __future__ import annotations
 
